+# Blog links in the user profile (MDL-88683)
+
+Documentation draft for the user-visible change introduced by MDL-88683.
+
+## Summary
+
+The Miscellaneous section of the user profile page now provides two blog links
+instead of one, giving Boost users a direct path to site-wide blog entries that
+previously required the Classic theme's Navigation block.
+
+## What changed
+
+When blogs are enabled on the site, the **Miscellaneous** section of a user
+profile (*User menu > Profile*, or any user's profile page) shows:
+
+- **View my blog entries** (on your own profile) - opens the list of your own
+  blog entries (`/blog/index.php?userid=<your id>`). On another user's profile
+  this link is still labelled **View all blog entries** and opens that user's
+  blog entries. This is the existing personal blog link, previously labelled
+  "Blog entries".
+- **View site blog entries** (new) - opens the site-wide blog listing
+  (`/blog/index.php`), showing all blog entries you are allowed to see.
+
+Both links appear in exactly the same situations where the personal blog link
+was shown before.
+
+## When the links are not shown
+
+- When blogs are disabled by the administrator (*Site administration >
+  Appearance > Blog > Enable blogs*), neither link is shown.
+- When the profile belongs to the guest user, neither link is shown.
+- When you are not allowed to view the profile owner's blog entries (for
+  example when blog visibility is set to "Users can only see their own blog"),
+  neither link is shown on that profile.
+
+## Unchanged behaviour
+
+- Blog pages, permissions, capabilities and visibility settings are unchanged.
+- Blog links in the Blog menu block and other blog blocks are unchanged.
