+@core @core_blog
+Feature: Blog links in the user profile
+  In order to reach my own and the site-wide blog entries
+  As a user
+  I need to be able to follow the blog links from the user profile
+
+  Background:
+    Given the following "users" exist:
+      | username  | firstname | lastname | email               |
+      | testuser  | Test      | User     | moodle@example.com  |
+      | testuser2 | Test2     | User2    | moodle2@example.com |
+    And the following "core_blog > entries" exist:
+      | subject               | body                     | user      |
+      | Blog post from user 1 | User 1 blog post content | testuser  |
+      | Blog post from user 2 | User 2 blog post content | testuser2 |
+
+  Scenario: View my own blog entries from the user profile
+    Given I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as testuser
+    And I should see "View my blog entries" in the "region-main" "region"
+    And I should see "View site blog entries" in the "region-main" "region"
+    When I follow "View my blog entries"
+    Then I should see "User blog: Test User"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 1"
+    And I should not see "Blog post from user 2"
+
+  Scenario: View site blog entries from the user profile
+    Given I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as testuser
+    When I follow "View site blog entries"
+    Then I should see "Site blog"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 1"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 2"
+
+  Scenario: View another user's blog entries from their profile
+    Given I am on the "testuser2" "user > profile" page logged in as testuser
+    And I should not see "View my blog entries" in the "region-main" "region"
+    And I should see "View site blog entries" in the "region-main" "region"
+    When I follow "View all blog entries"
+    Then I should see "User blog: Test2 User2"
+    And I should see "Blog post from user 2"
+    And I should not see "Blog post from user 1"
+
+  Scenario: Blog links are not shown in the user profile when blogs are disabled
+    Given the following config values are set as admin:
+      | enableblogs | 0 |
+    When I am on the "testuser" "user > profile" page logged in as testuser
+    Then I should not see "View my blog entries"
+    And I should not see "View site blog entries"
+    And I should not see "View all blog entries"
